          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.343,
            0.743,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": "5. When the light is incident along the normal on the mirror, which of the following statements is true:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.383,
            0.44,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": "(i) Angle of incidence is 90°"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.405,
            0.43,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Angle of incidence is 0°"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.427,
            0.44,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Angle of reflection is 90°"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.449,
            0.489,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": "(iv) No reflection of light takes place in this case"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.495,
            0.489,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": "6. Three mirrors—plane, concave and convex are placed in Fig. 10.25. On the basis of the images of the graph sheet formed in the mirrors, identify the mirrors and write their names above the mirrors."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.492,
            0.439,
            0.959,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.716,
                0.573,
                0.791,
                0.589
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 10.25"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.632,
            0.621,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": "7. In a museum, a woman walks towards a large concave mirror (Fig. 10.26). She will see that: (i) her erect image keeps decreasing in size."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.693,
            0.621,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": "(ii) her inverted image keeps decreasing in size."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.715,
            0.621,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": "(iii) her inverted image keeps increasing in size and eventually it becomes erect and magnified."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.774,
            0.594,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": "(iv) her erect image keeps increasing in size."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.801,
            0.622,
            0.858
          ],
          "content": "8. Hold a magnifying glass over text and identify the distance where you can see the text bigger than they are written. Now move it away"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.632,
            0.625,
